{"id": "159352", "revid": "1423298", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=159352", "title": "Llandudno (South Africa)", "text": "Llandudno is a residential suburb of Cape Town on the Atlantic Seaboard of the Western Cape. There are no shops or commercial activities, but the town has some of the most expensive residential property in South Africa."}
{"id": "159357", "revid": "144844", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=159357", "title": "La Punta", "text": "\"Not to be confused with San Giovanni La Punta in Catania, Sicily.\"\nLa Punta is the first Argentine city founded in the 21st century. It was founded\u00a0in March 2003 by the government of the province of San Luis.\nUnderstand.\nClimate.\nIn winter it is cold in the morning especially and in Summer there are cool breezes from the gorges.\nGet in.\nBy car, it is located 20 km north of San Luis Capital.\nGet around.\nLa Punta has a complete service structure conformed by hospital, school, police station, university, green spaces, and natural parks.\nSee.\nYou can visit the most modern technology center - The Data Center, The San Luis cinema set, the Astronomical Park Complex, the football stadium and the Educational Planet of the children. La Punta has a replica of the historical Cabildo of Buenos Aires, which was built in real scale with the appearance and materials that it had on May 25 1810 and Replica of the house of Tucum\u00e1n generating a true patriotic journey.\nDo.\nVisit Villa de la Quebrada for those who wish to discover the regional spirit, local beliefs and traditions.\nEat.\nIt does not have a variety of dining options but very close, in Potrero de los Funes, you can have access to good restaurants.\nSleep.\nThere is a great variety of accommodation in La Punta -Hotels, Bungalows and camping sites."}
{"id": "159373", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=159373", "title": "Cocentaina", "text": "Cocentaina is a town of 11,500 people (2018) in Alicante. It is known primarily for its textile industry, and tourists flock to experience its two festivals, both of them originating in the Middle Ages and declared 'Festivals of National Tourist Interest'.\nUnderstand.\nCocentaina (from Iberian: \"Contestani\" \u2013 the name of the regional Iberian tribe) has been inhabited since Paleolithic times, as attested by nearby cave paintings. Under Moorish rule \"Qustantaniya\" was an important enclave; the castle foundations, street layout, and numerous \"alquerias\" (fortified farmhouses) survive from that period. \nGet in.\nBy bus.\nAutocares Travicoi[dead link] (\u260f) runs several buses daily, including on weekends, between Valencia and Alcoy. From Alcoy, Subus (\u260f) runs buses multiple times daily; a summer schedule is available for download here[dead link] and a winter schedule is available here. Travicoi and Subus buses stop at in Cocentaina.\nBy car.\nCocentaina lies on the highway N-340 which connects to the A-7, running from Alicante to Alcoy and further on to Valencia.\nGet around.\nCocentaina is quite small, and easily navigable by foot.\nDrink.\nCocentaina, along with nearby Alcoy, is known for its caf\u00e9 licor ('coffee liquor'), not to be confused with the sweeter \"licor caf\u00e9\" in Murcia and Galicia. The drink is known to date to the early 13th century, and grew in popularity during the industrial revolution when factory workers would add it to their coffee thermoses. Today it has the Spanish denomination of origin of \"Bebidas Espirituosas Tradicionales\" ('Traditional Spirits'), and is consumed alone or mixed with other ingredients, such as \"orxata\" (Spanish: \"horchata\"), soda water, or lemon water.\nSleep.\nThere are just a couple hotels and a handful of holiday apartments in Cocentaina; more options are available in nearby Alcoy."}
{"id": "159416", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=159416", "title": "Portage (Michigan)", "text": "Portage is in Kalamazoo County in West Central Michigan. The population was 46,292 in the 2010 census. It is adjacent to Kalamazoo. Portage has miles of paths connecting its numerous parks.\nPortage once known for its production of celery continues to be a producer of various goods sitting at the intersection of US 131 and I-94 roughly halfway between Chicago and Detroit and a short drive to Grand Rapids and South Bend.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nPortage lies on Interstate 94 roughly mid-way between Chicago and Detroit and along US Highway 131 just south of Kalamazoo.\nBy bus.\nThe Kalamazoo downtown train station acts as the main regional bus station where you can change to the Kalamazoo Metro bus service to get to Portage."}
{"id": "159418", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=159418", "title": "La Seu d'Urgell", "text": "La Seu d'Urgell is in Lleida (province), Catalonia, Spain, very close to the border with Andorra. It has an Olympic-class pump-driven canoe and kayak sports venue adjacent to the historical centre of la Seu d'Urgell.\nUnderstand.\nThe city is at the confluence of two rivers, the Segre and Gran Valira, in a plain 7 km long and 691 m high surrounded by high mountains, such as the Cad\u00ed mountain range. The plain is called plana de la Seu and was formed by the Segre river.\nBecause it is at one of the major crossroads of communication in the Catalan Pyrenees, la Seu d'Urgell has had a unique and historic role in the county of Urgell. The roads to Andorra, Cerdanya and the low Segre all converge on la Seu d'Urgell.\nParallel to the Valira river rises a mountain range, where stand the remains of two great fortresses, the Ciutadella and Ciutat Castle (in Castellciutat), both of historic importance in the town. Small banks or open plains around the Segre are separated by gorges.\nIn the north, La Seu d'Urgell has borders with the municipality of les Valls de Valira, to the west with Montferrer i Castellb\u00f2 where there is La Seu d'Urgell Airport (also known as Andorra-Pirineus airport), to the south-west with Ribera d'Urgellet, to the south-east with Al\u00e0s i Cerc, and to the north-east with Estamariu."}
{"id": "159423", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=159423", "title": "Moscow/Central-East", "text": "Moscow Central-East (\u0426\u0435\u043d\u0442\u0440\u0430\u043b\u044c\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u041c\u043e\u0441\u043a\u043e\u0432\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439-\u0412\u043e\u0441\u0442\u043e\u043a) is in Moscow also part of Central Moscow."}
{"id": "159424", "revid": "1822", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=159424", "title": "Jorethang", "text": "Jorethang is a small town in South Sikkim.\nUnderstand.\nThe town has a population of around 10,000 and is located on the banks of the Rangeet River. While not a destination in itself, Jorethang is often used as a night halt by travellers heading to Pelling, Darjeeling and Siliguri.\nGet in.\nJeep-taxis ply the routes from Siliguri (three hours), Namchi (one hour) Darjeeling (90 minutes), Pelling (2 and half hours) and Tashiding (two hours)."}
